  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati Second Resilient Growth Development Policy Operation with a Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objectives and pillars of the Second Resilient Growth Development Policy Operation (DPO) with a Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option for Kiribati are to support the Government of Kiribati&apos;s (GOK) reforms to: (i) strengthen fiscal management, and (ii) promote inclusive and climate-resilient economic development. Strengthening fiscal management and promoting inclusive and climate resilient economic development are closely aligned with the GOK&apos;s key priorities. The prior actions in this DPO draw on lessons learned in previous Kiribati lending operations and from previous Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option (Cat DDOs) and include: (i) support should be coordinated amongst development partners; (ii) reforms should be spread across ministries to avoid overburdening any single one; (iii) technical assistance is needed to build capacity and improves the probability that reforms are successfully implemented; and (iv) reforms should be sequential, to help ensure they become embedded.</narrative>
  </description>
